# Commands that open a closed fold they move into ('foldopen', default
# "block,hor,mark,percent,quickfix,search,tag,undo"). A trailing j shows the fold is open.

=== a search into a closed fold opens it
ref:    options.txt *'foldopen'*
quote:  search search for a pattern: "/", "n", "*", "gd", etc.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
keys:   :2,4fold<CR>/three<CR>j
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |four
  five

=== n into a closed fold opens it
ref:    options.txt *'foldopen'*
quote:  search search for a pattern: "/", "n", "*", "gd", etc.
given:
  |x one
  two
  x three
  four
  x five
keys:   /x<CR>:2,4fold<CR>ggnj
expect:
  x one
  two
  x three
  |four
  x five

=== a search from a closed fold skips matches in it
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  When starting a search in a closed fold it will not find a match in the current fold.
given:
  one
  |x two
  x three
  four
  x five
keys:   :2,4fold<CR>/x<CR>
expect:
  one
  x two
  x three
  four
  |x five

=== a backward search from a closed fold starts at its first line
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  a backwards search starts from the start of the closed fold.
given:
  x one
  two
  x three
  |four
  five
keys:   :2,4fold<CR>?x<CR>
expect:
  |x one
  two
  x three
  four
  five

=== l in a closed fold opens it
ref:    options.txt *'foldopen'*
quote:  hor horizontal movements: "l", "w", "fx", etc.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>lj
expect:
  one
  two
  t|hree
  four

=== % into a closed fold opens it
ref:    options.txt *'foldopen'*
quote:  percent "%"
given:
  one
  |two (
  three
  four )
  five
keys:   :2,4fold<CR>%j
expect:
  one
  two (
  three
  four )
  fiv|e

=== } into a closed fold opens it
ref:    options.txt *'foldopen'*
quote:  block "(", "{", "[[", "[{", etc.
given:
  |one
  two
  
  four
  five
keys:   :2,4fold<CR>}j
expect:
  one
  two
  
  |four
  five

=== 'a into a closed fold opens it
ref:    options.txt *'foldopen'*
quote:  mark jumping to a mark: "'m", CTRL-O, etc.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
keys:   jjma:2,4fold<CR>gg'aj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |four
  five

=== `a into a closed fold opens it
ref:    options.txt *'foldopen'*
quote:  mark jumping to a mark: "'m", CTRL-O, etc.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
keys:   jjlma:2,4fold<CR>gg`aj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  f|our
  five

=== CTRL-O into a closed fold opens it
ref:    options.txt *'foldopen'*
quote:  mark jumping to a mark: "'m", CTRL-O, etc.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
keys:   3G:2,4fold<CR>gg<C-o>j
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |four
  five

=== u opens the fold holding the change
ref:    options.txt *'foldopen'*
quote:  undo undo or redo: "u" and CTRL-R
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
keys:   jjx:2,4fold<CR>gguj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |four
  five

=== CTRL-R opens the fold holding the change
ref:    options.txt *'foldopen'*
quote:  undo undo or redo: "u" and CTRL-R
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
keys:   jjxu:2,4fold<CR>gg<C-r>j
expect:
  one
  two
  hree
  |four
  five

=== inserting in a closed fold opens it
ref:    options.txt *'foldopen'*
quote:  In insert mode the folds containing the cursor will always be open when text is inserted.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>ix<Esc>j
expect:
  one
  xtwo
  |three
  four

=== an operator with a search into a closed fold leaves it closed
ref:    options.txt *'foldopen'*
quote:  When a movement command is used for an operator (e.g., "dl" or "y%") this option is not used.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>y/four<CR>jjj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  |five

=== a search into a closed fold is a jump
ref:    options.txt *'foldopen'*
quote:  search search for a pattern: "/", "n", "*", "gd", etc.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
keys:   :2,4fold<CR>/three<CR>
expect:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
jumps:  1:0

=== G into a closed fold is a jump
ref:    options.txt *'foldopen'*
quote:  jump far jumps: "G", "gg", etc.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
keys:   :2,4fold<CR>G
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |four
jumps:  1:0
